From: erenmakal <69559506+erenmakal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 02:01:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix spawnRadius zero ignoring setworldspawn

Based on PaperMC/Folia PR #475. When spawnRadius is zero, Folia's random spawn
helper can fall back to the world-border center rather than the configured
world spawn. Preserve the exact configured spawn in that case.


diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
@@ -3242,6 +3242,12 @@ public class ServerPlayer extends Player implements ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patc
         BlockPos spawn = world.getLevelData().getRespawnData().pos();
         double radius = Math.max(0.0, world.getGameRules().get(GameRules.RESPAWN_RADIUS).doubleValue());
 
+        // Folia performance pack - PaperMC/Folia #401 / PR #475
+        if (dev.eren.folia.config.FoliaConfig.fixSpawnRadiusZero && radius <= 0.0) {
+            return spawn;
+        }
+
         double spawnX = (double)spawn.getX() + 0.5;
         double spawnZ = (double)spawn.getZ() + 0.5;
